  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14214505/assets/24ee434f11bca408587e1baa6b9189e430fa745cef0668bc35cd871761f410ed.png)\n\nThe function $h(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-3,5].$ The graph of ${h}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $h(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $2,$ $6,$ and $4$ respectively (from left to right). Find the maximum value of $h(x)$ on the interval $[-3,5]$ given that $h(3)=2.$\n\n${h}_{\\text{max}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
